<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="ChatGPT" version="31.4.2">
<diagram id="opentwin-rv-reqs" name="Requirements Specification">
<mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1400" pageHeight="3092" math="0" shadow="0">
<root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="S0" value="OpenTwin Modular Amphibious RV — High-Level Requirements Engineering Specification&#xa;&#xa;Concept baseline • Open modular architecture • Digital-twin enabled • Engineering targets, not certification claims." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;fontStyle=1;fontSize=18;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="30" width="1220" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S1" value="1. Mission &amp; Scope&#xa;&#xa;SYS-001 SHALL operate as a road-towable recreational living module and protected-water houseboat.&#xa;SYS-002 SHALL separate road, marine, habitation, energy and digital-twin subsystem boundaries.&#xa;SYS-003 SHALL use replaceable interfaces to minimize proprietary lock-in.&#xa;SYS-004 SHALL support configurable variants without changing the core architecture." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="160" width="1220" height="166" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S0" target="S1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S2" value="2. Stakeholders &amp; CONOPS&#xa;&#xa;STK-001 Occupants: habitation, comfort, access and emergency egress.&#xa;STK-002 Tow operator: coupling, transport configuration, braking/lighting and status.&#xa;STK-003 Marine operator: launch/recovery, maneuvering, navigation and docking.&#xa;STK-004 Maintainer: diagnostics, service access and replaceable modules.&#xa;OPS-001 Road → launch → marine operation → docking → recovery → road.&#xa;OPS-002 Support off-grid habitation and intermittent communications." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="356" width="1220" height="214" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S1" target="S2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S3" value="3. Vehicle / Marine Platform&#xa;&#xa;MEC-001 SHALL carry defined road, launch, marine and habitation load cases.&#xa;MEC-002 Hull SHALL provide watertight integrity, drainage and inspectable penetrations.&#xa;MEC-003 SHALL maintain mass, payload and center-of-gravity budgets.&#xa;MAR-001 SHALL provide propulsion, steering, docking and emergency shutdown.&#xa;MAR-002 Stability, buoyancy and freeboard SHALL be verified for approved loading conditions.&#xa;ROAD-001 Define towing envelope, hitch loads, dimensions and road interfaces." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="600" width="1220" height="214" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S2" target="S3"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S4" value="4. Energy &amp; Propulsion&#xa;&#xa;ENE-001 SHALL use modular protected DC energy storage/distribution.&#xa;ENE-002 Photovoltaics SHALL connect through a documented power-management boundary.&#xa;ENE-003 Shore charging SHALL include required electrical protection/isolation.&#xa;ENE-004 Critical loads SHALL be prioritized under degraded energy.&#xa;PRP-001 Electric propulsion SHALL expose command, state, fault and energy telemetry.&#xa;PRP-002 Emergency isolation SHALL not depend on cloud connectivity." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="844" width="1220" height="214" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S3" target="S4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S5" value="5. Habitation &amp; Utilities&#xa;&#xa;HAB-001 SHALL provide sleeping, seating, food-preparation, sanitation and storage for approved occupancy.&#xa;HAB-002 SHALL provide ventilation, thermal management, lighting and emergency egress.&#xa;WTR-001 SHALL separate potable, grey and waste systems with serviceable tanks and monitoring.&#xa;FIR-001 Fire strategy SHALL address batteries, galley and electrical equipment.&#xa;HMI-001 Local controls SHALL remain usable without remote services." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1088" width="1220" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S4" target="S5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S6" value="6. OpenTwin Digital Twin&#xa;&#xa;DT-001 SHALL assign unique digital identities to the RV and major replaceable subsystems.&#xa;DT-002 Twin state SHALL represent location, energy, propulsion, water, environment and equipment health.&#xa;DT-003 Telemetry SHALL include timestamp, units, quality/status and provenance.&#xa;DT-004 Historical state and maintenance events SHALL be auditable.&#xa;EDGE-001 Essential monitoring/control SHALL operate locally when disconnected.&#xa;EDGE-002 Cloud/AI SHALL NOT be a single point of failure for safety-critical functions." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1308" width="1220" height="214" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E6" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S5" target="S6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S7" value="7. Open Interfaces &amp; Data&#xa;&#xa;INT-001 SHALL publish versioned contracts for power, telemetry, commands and service data.&#xa;INT-002 SHALL prefer open protocols/formats; adapters SHALL isolate vendor-specific implementations.&#xa;INT-003 SHOULD support REST/OpenAPI and event/telemetry interfaces such as MQTT where appropriate.&#xa;INT-004 SHALL support owner-authorized export in documented machine-readable formats.&#xa;INT-005 SHALL define compatibility/versioning rules for independently implemented modules." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1552" width="1220" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E7" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S6" target="S7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S8" value="8. Safety, Cybersecurity &amp; Privacy&#xa;&#xa;SAF-001 SHALL perform hazard analysis for road, marine, electrical, fire, flooding and human factors.&#xa;SAF-002 Safety-critical functions SHALL enter defined safe/degraded states on faults.&#xa;CYB-001 SHALL authenticate users/devices and apply least privilege.&#xa;CYB-002 SHALL protect communications, secrets, updates and audit records.&#xa;CYB-003 SHOULD segment safety/vehicle networks from infotainment/external services.&#xa;PRV-001 Location/occupant data SHALL support minimization, retention controls and authorization." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="1772" width="1220" height="214" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E8" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S7" target="S8"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S9" value="9. Verification &amp; Traceability&#xa;&#xa;VER-001 Each normative requirement SHALL have ID, rationale, owner, verification method and acceptance criterion.&#xa;VER-002 Methods: Inspection (I), Analysis (A), Demonstration (D), Test (T).&#xa;VER-003 SHALL maintain need ↔ requirement ↔ subsystem ↔ verification-evidence traceability.&#xa;VER-004 SHALL validate roadworthiness, marine stability/handling, electrical safety, watertightness, EMC and habitability against applicable jurisdictional requirements.&#xa;VER-005 SHALL test twin accuracy, latency, offline behavior and recovery." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="2016" width="1220" height="190" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E9" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S8" target="S9"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S10" value="10. Engineering Budgets / TBD&#xa;&#xa;TBD-001 Road dimensions and gross trailer mass.&#xa;TBD-002 Occupancy and payload.&#xa;TBD-003 Displacement, draft, freeboard and stability criteria.&#xa;TBD-004 Propulsion power, target speed and endurance.&#xa;TBD-005 Battery usable energy, PV peak power and reserve policy.&#xa;TBD-006 Potable/grey/waste capacities and autonomy.&#xa;TBD-007 Temperature, wind, wave and water-condition envelope.&#xa;TBD-008 Target jurisdictions and applicable standards." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="2236" width="1220" height="262" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E10" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S9" target="S10"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S11" value="11. Open Design / IP Position&#xa;&#xa;IP-001 Architecture SHALL be modular and implementation-independent where feasible.&#xa;IP-002 Third-party components SHALL record source, version, license and interface obligations.&#xa;IP-003 Prefer openly documented interfaces and independently replaceable components.&#xa;NOTE: Open-source licensing does not itself guarantee freedom from third-party patent or other IP rights; jurisdiction-specific review remains required." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="2528" width="1220" height="166" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E11" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S10" target="S11"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="S12" value="12. Requirements Baseline Exit Criteria&#xa;&#xa;BASE-001 Stakeholders and CONOPS approved.&#xa;BASE-002 System boundary/interfaces baselined.&#xa;BASE-003 Critical TBDs resolved or assigned owners/dates.&#xa;BASE-004 Preliminary hazard analysis completed.&#xa;BASE-005 Requirements traceability matrix established.&#xa;BASE-006 Verification plan mapped to SHALL requirements.&#xa;BASE-007 Architecture ready for Preliminary Design Review (PDR)." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=12;fontSize=15;strokeWidth=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="80" y="2724" width="1220" height="238" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="E12" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="S11" target="S12"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root>
</mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
</mxfile>